alue \"no cable\" per text. I'll use \"none\".\n\nLet me now also double-check e for both = 1 g: table \"e = | 1 g | 1 g\". Yes → type_level.\n\nd: \"d = | 0.1 g | 1 g\". Yes.\n\nNow description field — I'll write a thorough description.\n\nAlso \"The instrument shall not be used for direct sales to the public.\" Include.\n\nNow build the final JSON. Let me be careful with the ordering of keys following schema: certificate, issuing_authority, applicants, manufacturers, certified_type, model_family, components, characteristics, matrix_tables (skip), recommendation, test_reports, revision_history, footnotes (skip).\n\ncertified_type.type_designations: include PMA-EV, PMA-HD and all 38 models. That's 40 entries.\n\nmodel_family:\n```json\n{\n  \"family_name\": null,\n  \"models\": [ ...38 entries... ]\n}\n```\nEach entry: {\"model_id\": \"...\", \"label\": \"PMA-EV\", \"attributes\": {\"instrument_type\": \"PMA-EV\", \"accuracy_class\": \"II\", \"environment\": \"standard\", \"rj45_cable_length\": {\"value\": \"none\"}}}\n\nHmm label — maybe label should be something descriptive like \"PMA-EV paint-mixing scale, Class II\". I'll set label to the instrument type \"PMA-EV\". Fine.\n\nLet me write out all models with attributes:\n\n1. EVO1S1N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, standard, none\n2. EVO1S1CI-C: PMA-EV, II, standard, none\n3. EVO1Y1N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, none\n4. EVO1Y1CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, none\n5. EVO1X1N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, none\n6. EVO1X1CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, none\n7. EVO1X2N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 10 m\n8. EVO1X2CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 10 m\n9. EVO1X3N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 20 m\n10. EVO1X3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 20 m\n11. EVO1X4N3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 30 m\n12. EVO1X4CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 1, 30 m\n13. VIS1Y1M3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, none\n14. VIS1Y1CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, none\n15. VIS1Y2M3CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, 10 m\n16. VIS1Y2CI-C: PMA-EV, II, Ex-zone 2, 10 m\n17. VIS1Y3M3CI-C: PMA-EV, II,